Third-party components:

- gtnh-factory-flow (https://github.com/Samiracle64/gtnh-factory-flow), MIT License.
  gtnh_solver consumes plan/recipe JSON EXPORTED by gtnh-factory-flow as input. No
  gtnh-factory-flow source code is included or vendored in this repository; only the
  user's exported data files are read at runtime. GTNH recipe/texture data carried in
  those exports remains under its respective owners' licenses.

- GT5-Unofficial (https://github.com/GTNewHorizons/GT5-Unofficial) and StructureLib
  (https://github.com/GTNewHorizons/StructureLib), both LGPL, GTNewHorizons. The
  dataset-extraction tool under tools/gtnh-extractor depends on these as unmodified
  library dependencies (pulled from the GTNH Nexus) to run a headless server and read
  back multiblock structure facts. No GT5-Unofficial or StructureLib source is vendored
  or patched here. Extracted structure facts are committed to this repository; GT's
  textures (LGPL, like its code) are not vendored and are fetched from the mod jar at
  build time. Specifically, the 3D previewer (src/gtnh_solver/previewer) fetches the
  pinned GT5-Unofficial jar from the GTNH Nexus at preview time, caches it outside the
  repository, extracts the referenced iconset PNGs, and embeds them (as data: URIs) only
  in the generated preview HTML. No PNG is ever committed to this repository.

- Applied Energistics 2 Unofficial
  (https://github.com/GTNewHorizons/Applied-Energistics-2-Unofficial), GTNewHorizons' fork
  of Applied Energistics 2, (c) 2013 - 2015 AlgorithmX2 et al. Its code is LGPL-3.0 and its
  API MIT, but its textures and models are licensed under Creative Commons
  Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 3.0 (CC BY-NC-SA 3.0,
  https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/3.0/). AE2FluidCraft-Rework
  (https://github.com/GTNewHorizons/AE2FluidCraft-Rework), GTNewHorizons, LGPL-3.0.
  data/ae2/<AE2 version>/render.json holds geometry numbers and texture names that
  tools/derive_ae_render.py reads from both mods' source at the tags pinned in
  src/gtnh_solver/dataset/mod_jars.py; no source, texture or model of either mod is vendored
  here. The previewer fetches both pinned jars from the GTNH Nexus at preview time when a
  page needs their art (an ME network, or a GT block that wears AE2 art), as it does
  GT5-Unofficial's, caches them outside the repository and reads the PNGs a preview draws; no
  PNG is ever committed. A preview HTML that embeds AE2 textures redistributes
  CC BY-NC-SA 3.0 art: it may be shared for non-commercial purposes only, with this
  attribution and the licence link above, and an adaptation of that art must be shared under
  the same licence. Every such preview shows that attribution, the licence link and the
  non-commercial terms on the page itself. AE2FluidCraft declares LGPL-3.0 for all of its
  files, but whether any of its textures derive from AE2's art has not been checked, so a
  preview that embeds AE2FluidCraft textures is shared on the same CC BY-NC-SA 3.0 terms.

- NESQL Exporter (https://github.com/ShadowTheAge/nesql-exporter, a fork of
  https://github.com/D-Cysteine/nesql-exporter), LGPL-3.0. tools/derive_icons.py reads the
  database script and image archive the exporter writes when run in a GT:NH instance. The
  exporter is built and run separately, from the build-file-only fork pinned in
  gtnh.lock.json (https://github.com/MrBruh/nesql-exporter); none of its source is vendored
  here, and the icons it renders are local data, never committed to this repository.

- GTNH Calculator (https://github.com/ShadowTheAge/gtnh), MIT License, Copyright (c) 2025
  ShadowTheAge. src/gtnh_solver/dataset/nesql.py carries, as Python, the table from its
  export/FontCharactersFixer.cs that maps GT:NH's private-use font glyphs to the Unicode
  symbols they are drawn as. No other part of it is included. The optional `shadow` extra
  installs gtnh-shadow-convert (https://github.com/MrBruh/gtnh-shadow-convert, MIT), a separate
  package that ports the calculator's data reader, solver and machine rules to read its plans.
  examples/Shadow-NB.gtnh is a plan the calculator saved (recipe ids, tiers and options only),
  and examples/shadow-nitrobenzene.json is that plan converted. The calculator's recipe data
  (data.bin, from https://github.com/ShadowTheAge/gtnh-data) is published without a license and
  is never included in this repository; a user downloads it separately. Its license:

